# EF Core 10 Breaking Changes for Your Code

## 1. `SetProperty` — value parameter must be a lambda expression

In EF Core 10, the `SetProperty` overload accepting a raw value/constant was removed. The value argument must now be an `Expression<Func<TSource, TProperty>>` lambda.

**Fix:** Wrap `Expression.Constant("foo")` in a lambda:

```csharp
var blogParameter = Expression.Parameter(typeof(Blog), "b");
var valueParam = Expression.Parameter(typeof(Blog), "v");

setters = Expression.Lambda<Func<SetPropertyCalls<Blog>, SetPropertyCalls<Blog>>>(
    Expression.Call(
        instance: setters.Body,
        methodName: nameof(SetPropertyCalls<Blog>.SetProperty),
        typeArguments: new[] { typeof(string) },
        arguments: new Expression[]
        {
            Expression.Lambda<Func<Blog, string>>(
                Expression.Property(blogParameter, nameof(Blog.Name)), blogParameter),
            // NEW: value must be a lambda, not a bare constant
            Expression.Lambda<Func<Blog, string>>(
                Expression.Constant("foo"), valueParam)
        }),
    setters.Parameters);
```

---

## 2. Complex types — duplicate CLR types require explicit property configuration

EF Core 10 requires explicit column naming/discrimination when multiple complex properties share the same CLR type. Nested complex types must also be explicitly configured on the inner builder.

**Fix:**

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, ab =>
    {
        ab.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingStreet");
    });
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, ab =>
    {
        ab.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("BillingStreet");
    });
});

// Nested complex types: configure each level explicitly
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment, pb =>
    {
        pb.ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress, ab =>
        {
            ab.Property(a => a.City).HasColumnName("PaymentCity");
        });
    });
});
```

---

## 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `CommandSource` parameter

EF Core 10 adds a `CommandSource commandSource` parameter to the diagnostic methods.

**Fix:**

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        CommandSource commandSource)   // <-- new required parameter
    { /* logging */ }
}
```

---

**Summary of actions:**
| Area | Change |
|------|--------|
| `SetProperty` expression trees | Wrap value in `Expression.Lambda<Func<T,TProp>>(...)` |
| Duplicate complex types | Add explicit `HasColumnName` or column prefix per property |
| `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` | Add `CommandSource commandSource` to all method signatures |
